---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout pageTitle="Terms of Use">
  <section class="legal">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="legal-date">Last updated: August 2026</p>

    <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
    <p>
      By creating an account or installing the The Virtue Initiative client, you agree to these
      Terms of Use. If you do not agree, do not use the service.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Description of service</h2>
    <p>
      The Virtue Initiative is a free, non-profit pornography accountability tool. Its client
      applications for Linux, macOS, Windows, Android, and iOS may capture screenshots, monitor
      device or system state, analyze screenshots on your device to estimate concern, and send
      encrypted monitoring data and the metadata needed to index and summarize it to the service, so
      that information can be made available to you and the accountability partners you designate.
      The service may also email you and your partners alerts and periodic summaries, subject to the
      preferences you set. The Virtue Initiative is operated as a non-profit project, provided free
      of charge, and may change as the software continues to develop.
    </p>
    <p>
      Concern scoring is automated and imperfect. It will miss some content and flag some content
      wrongly, and it is not a substitute for your own judgment or your partners'. Nothing about the
      service should be relied on as a complete or accurate record of what happened on a device.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 13 years of age to use The Virtue Initiative. By using the service you
      represent that you meet this requirement.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Your account</h2>
    <p>
      You are responsible for maintaining the security of your account credentials. You are
      responsible for all activity that occurs under your account. Notify us immediately at <a
        href="mailto:help@virtueinitiative.org">help@virtueinitiative.org</a
      > if you suspect unauthorized access.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Use the service for any unlawful purpose or in violation of any applicable United States
        law.
      </li>
      <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to other users' accounts or data.</li>
      <li>Interfere with or disrupt the integrity or performance of the service.</li>
      <li>
        Use the service to capture or share screenshots of individuals without complying with
        applicable law or, where required, without their knowledge or consent.
      </li>
      <li>
        Use the service in a way that violates platform rules, workplace policies, school policies,
        or other obligations that apply to you.
      </li>
      <li>
        Invite someone as an accountability partner using an email address you do not have their
        permission to use, or submit bug reports abusively or in bulk.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Accountability partners</h2>
    <p>
      When you invite an accountability partner and they accept, you grant them the ability to
      decrypt and view your monitoring data, and they receive alert and summary emails about your
      account. You are responsible for choosing your partners, understanding what access you are
      granting, and managing that access appropriately. Removing a partner stops their access to
      data captured afterward; it cannot undo access to data they could already decrypt.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Donations</h2>
    <p>
      Donations are voluntary and are not required to use the service; donating grants no additional
      features, access, or rights. Donations are processed by Stripe and are subject to Stripe's own
      terms. Donations are generally non-refundable, though you may contact us about a donation made
      in error. If you set up a recurring donation, it continues until you cancel it; you may cancel
      at any time by contacting us. We are a non-profit project - contact us if you need a receipt,
      and consult your own advisor about the tax treatment of your donation.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Bug reports</h2>
    <p>
      When you submit a bug report you may include a description, a contact email address, and, from
      a client app, a recent excerpt of that device's operational log. The app tells you before it
      attaches logs. If you are signed in, or reporting from a client app signed in to your account,
      the report always identifies your account; it is not anonymous. Do not include information in
      a report that you do not want us to receive. We use reports to diagnose problems and to reply
      to you, and we handle them as described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Data and privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Your use of The Virtue Initiative is also governed by our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a
      >, which is incorporated into these Terms by reference.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Open source</h2>
    <p>
      The Virtue Initiative software is intended to remain open source and self-hostable. Use,
      copying, modification, and distribution of the source code are governed by the license terms
      that apply to the repository and its components. These Terms govern use of the hosted service
      operated by us.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
    <p>
      The Virtue Initiative is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind, express or implied.
      We do not warrant that the service will be uninterrupted, error-free, or that data will not be
      lost. Use the service at your own risk.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, The Virtue Initiative shall not be liable for any
      indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising out of or related to
      your use of the service.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Termination</h2>
    <p>
      You may stop using the service at any time. You may delete your hosted account and its
      associated data yourself from the web app's settings, or request deletion by contacting us;
      encrypted monitoring data is removed on the schedule described in the
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. We reserve the right to suspend or terminate accounts
      that violate these Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of New York, without regard to its conflict
      of laws rules. You and we agree that any dispute arising out of or relating to these Terms or
      the service shall be brought exclusively in the state or federal courts located in New York,
      and you consent to the personal jurisdiction of those courts.
    </p>

    <h2>15. Changes to these Terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes will be communicated by updating
      the "Last updated" date above. Continued use of the service after changes constitutes
      acceptance of the revised Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>16. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For questions about these Terms, contact us at <a href="mailto:help@virtueinitiative.org"
        >help@virtueinitiative.org</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
